# UST.G3AY Relative Gram-Jet and Unit-Screening Theorem

## Purpose

G3AX defines the normalized top functional over the complete rank-123
graph-preserving residue ball, while G3AW needs only six scalar contractions.
This theorem compiles those scalar values and their full first jet without a
symbolic inverse of the 39,725-square minor. It also identifies the exact
finite-residue test that can certify Gram nondegeneracy uniformly over the
whole ball.

## Relative scalar formula

Write the G3AX normalization system as

```text
B(u)x(u)+c(u)=0,          x(u)=t(u)[J],
t(u)[j_*]=1,              j_*=28267.
```

For one G3AW product vector `p_a(u)`, split its coordinates as
`(p_a,*,p_a,J)` and set

```text
h_a(u)=p_a,*(u)+p_a,J(u)^T x(u).
```

Solve the adjoint system

```text
B(u)^T y_a(u)=p_a,J(u).
```

Then

```text
h_a(u)=p_a,*(u)-y_a(u)^T c(u).
```

For a tangent direction `delta`, implicit differentiation gives

```text
D_delta h_a
 = D_delta p_a,* + (D_delta p_a,J)^T x
   - y_a^T((D_delta B)x+D_delta c).                 (1)
```

Equation (1) uses matrix-vector products after the base and adjoint solves;
it does not require a separate solve for each of the 123 directions.

## Solve count

After one reusable exact factorization of `B(u)`:

```text
forward sensitivities for 123 directions: 1+123 = 124 RHS solves,
adjoints for six Gram outputs:             1+6   =   7 RHS solves.
```

Thus the six-output full Jacobian removes 117 large right-hand-side solves.
For a general `d`-direction, `m`-output batch, choose the smaller of the
forward and adjoint routes: `1+min(d,m)` solves after factorization.

## Finite unit screen

All graph-ball members reduce to the same G3AP functional. If the transported
product vectors are emitted through an exact DVR reduction or an independently
certified finite common-frame transport, the six contractions reduce to one
matrix `H_0` over `F_(101^6)`. Therefore:

- a nonzero diagonal entry of `H_0` is a unit for every integral lift;
- `det(H_0) != 0` proves the Gram span nondegenerate for every lift;
- a nonidentity reduced reflection word proves the characteristic-zero word
  is nonidentity.

An ordinary floating-point or interval-complex transport is not such an input:
there is no automatic componentwise reduction from complex numerics to this
finite field. G3AZ makes the accepted source contract executable.

The converses are false. A zero residue entry may acquire a nonzero higher
digit, and a reduced identity word needs a characteristic-zero lift. The
screen is therefore a rigorous unit/no-go shortcut, not an endpoint theorem.

## Execution consequence

When the three G3AT transports finish, first establish an exact DVR/finite
comparison into the locked G3AP carrier, or evaluate the six
characteristic-zero pairings directly. For an admissible finite input, if the
three diagonals and determinant are nonzero, G3AW
nondegeneracy is closed uniformly before member selection. For any remaining
same-member scalar or derivative calculation, factor the selected G3AX minor
once and use the seven-solve adjoint compiler.

The required heavy artifact is now a reusable exact unit-pivot solver oracle,
not a symbolic 39,725-square inverse and not 124 unrelated eliminations.

## Proof boundary

G3AY does not emit the transported vectors, six Gram values, factorization,
member, meridian, `beta_C` or endpoint. It does not infer nonzero from a zero
residue value. It changes the exact execution algorithm and supplies a
uniform promotion rule for future nonzero modular Gram data.

